  "7d9ij": "The smallest network with every ingredient of deep learning: Linear layers alternating with activation functions, softmax and cross-entropy at the end, and an optimizer that updates the weights along the gradient. The network trains right in the page: the forward pass computes predictions, the backward pass computes gradients with the chain rule from the last layer back to the first, and the optimizer takes one small step down the slope of the loss.", // Mạng nhỏ nhất có đủ các thành phần của học sâu: các lớp Linear xen kẽ…
  "u2xipz": "The learning rate η is the most important knob: too small and learning is very slow, too large and each step leaps across the whole valley of the loss. Adam scales the step of each parameter by the size of its recent gradients, so it is less sensitive to η than SGD. Hidden layers and nonlinearities are what let the network draw curved boundaries; the number of neurons decides how intricate the boundary can get. But the freer the boundary, the more easily the network memorizes even the wrong labels: the test set, never used for learning, is the only way to know whether the network generalizes. Training loss still falling while the test loss rises is overfitting. Weight decay pulls every weight a little towards 0 at each step, pushing the network towards a simpler boundary; mini-batches make each step cheaper but noisier.", // Learning rate η là núm quan trọng nhất: quá nhỏ thì học rất chậm, quá…
  "a3f653": "Measured on this very page (\"Circles\" dataset, 8 neurons, ReLU): Adam with η = 0.03 brings the loss below 0.1 in 40 steps; SGD with the same η is still at 0.145 after 600 steps; η = 3 kills every ReLU, the loss gets stuck at 0.693 and the accuracy at 50%. \"Spiral\" dataset: 8 neurons stall around 94%, 16 neurons reach 100% after about 180 steps. \"Circles\" with 16 neurons and 20% of the training labels flipped: the lowest test loss, about 0.18, comes in the first steps; after 2,000 steps it has climbed to 0.35–0.6 while the training loss is down to about 0.15–0.2 (the exact numbers differ between browsers, because Adam amplifies rounding errors); add weight decay λ = 0.1 and the test loss stays around 0.25, with about 92% of the test set right.", // Đo trên chính trang này (bộ "Vòng tròn", 8 neuron, ReLU): Adam với η …
