  "dwou0z": "A decoder-only language model: it reads a sequence of tokens, guesses the next token, appends the guess and repeats. This is the architecture of most LLMs today. Compared with the original Transformer: no encoder and no cross-attention, normalization before each sublayer, RMSNorm instead of LayerNorm, RoPE instead of PE, SwiGLU instead of ReLU, and groups of Q heads sharing K and V (GQA).", // Mô hình ngôn ngữ chỉ có decoder: đọc một chuỗi token, đoán token kế t…
  "ihlvw4": "A single simple objective, guessing the next token, but on an enormous amount of text (LLaMA 3 was trained on more than 15 trillion tokens), is enough for the model to learn grammar, knowledge and even reasoning. No encoder is needed because plain text has no source–target pairs: everything is one long sequence. GPT-2 (2019) uses the same frame, but with LayerNorm, a learned PE and GELU.", // Chỉ một mục tiêu đơn giản là đoán token kế tiếp, nhưng trên lượng văn…
