  "l253wc": "The second line is why RoPE is neat: the dot product of a query at position \\(m\\) and a key at position \\(n\\) depends only on the distance \\(n - m\\), not on the absolute positions. The same \"clock hand\" idea as the original Transformer's sin/cos PE, but applied to Q and K by multiplication instead of being added to the input. LLaMA 3 uses a base of 500,000 (LLaMA 2: 10,000) so the hands turn more slowly, which suits long contexts.", // Dòng thứ hai là lý do RoPE hay: tích vô hướng giữa query ở vị trí \(m…
