  "1xzhpk8": "Suppose the components of \\(q, k\\) are independent, with mean 0 and variance 1. Then \\(q \\cdot k\\) has variance \\(d_k = 128\\), a standard deviation of \\(\\sqrt{128} \\approx 11.31\\). A softmax over numbers that far apart is nearly one-hot, the gradient through it is close to 0, and the network learns very slowly. Dividing by \\(\\sqrt{d_k}\\) brings the variance back to 1.", // Giả sử các thành phần của \(q, k\) độc lập, trung bình 0, phương sai …
